\id LUK - Test Project
\h Luke
\toc1 The Gospel of Luke
\mt1 Luke
\c 1
\p
\v 1 Many have undertaken to compile a narrative about the events that have been fulfilled among us.
\v 2 Just as the original eyewitnesses and servants of the word handed them down to us.
\v 3 It also seemed good to me, since I have investigated everything carefully from the very first, to write to you in orderly sequence, most honorable Theophilus.
\v 4 So that you may know the certainty of the things about which you have been instructed.
\v 5 In the days of King Herod of Judea, there was a priest named Zechariah.
\c 2
\p
\v 1 In those days a decree went out from Caesar Augustus that all the world should be registered.
\v 2 This was the first registration; it took place while Quirinius was governing Syria.
\v 3 Everyone went to be registered, each to his own town.
\v 4 Joseph also went up from Galilee, out of the town of Nazareth, into Judea, to the city of David.
